<mxCell id="c306" value="External (CRM.partners/leads, SCHEDULE.sched_items, Laravel users)" style="text;html=1;fontSize=12;fontColor=#12181F;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="72" y="1493" width="700" height="24" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
<mxCell id="c307" value="FK* = real cross-schema FKs into &quot;CRM&quot;.partners(id)/&quot;CRM&quot;.leads(id)/&quot;SCHEDULE&quot;.sched_items(id)/public.users(id) — safe because this is Vertical depending on Core (§5), the only allowed direction; those Core modules have zero knowledge of LEGAL.*. deed_parties.identity_snapshot is a point-in-time COPY of CRM.partners data at signing, never a live reference (§3J/§5) — a later CRM edit must never silently change a signed deed. deeds.amends_deed_id and bpn_submissions.resubmission_of_id are the non-destructive-correction pattern: a correction is always a new linked row, never an edit-in-place. protocol_entries is enforced append-only by a real Postgres trigger (like INVENTORY.stock_ledger), since a Notaris is personally liable for this specific ledger." style="text;html=1;fontSize=11;fontColor=#4A5563;align=left;fontStyle=2;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="40" y="1542" width="1500" height="70" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
      </root>
    </mxGraphModel>
  </diagram>
</mxfile>
